       The ggeettsseerrvveenntt() function reads the next entry from the services  data‐
       base  (see  sseerrvviicceess(5)) and returns a _s_e_r_v_e_n_t structure containing the
       broken‐out fields from the entry.  A connection is opened to the  data‐
       base if necessary.

       The  ggeettsseerrvvbbyynnaammee() function returns a _s_e_r_v_e_n_t structure for the entry
       from the database that matches the service _n_a_m_e using  protocol  _p_r_o_t_o.
       If _p_r_o_t_o is NULL, any protocol will be matched.  A connection is opened
       to the database if necessary.

       The  ggeettsseerrvvbbyyppoorrtt() function returns a _s_e_r_v_e_n_t structure for the entry
       from the database that matches the port _p_o_r_t (given in network byte or‐
       der) using protocol _p_r_o_t_o.  If _p_r_o_t_o is  NULL,  any  protocol  will  be
       matched.  A connection is opened to the database if necessary.

